Wait, `D1` in `game/collisions.test.js` is still failing!
```javascript
test('D1: Ball should bounce off brick (not just pass through)', () => {
  const state = createState(1);
  const brick = state.bricks[0];
  state.ball.x = brick.x + BRICK_W / 2;
  state.ball.y = brick.y - 8;
  state.ball.vx = 0;
  state.ball.vy = 100;

  state.ball.y += state.ball.vy * 0.02;
  const oldVy = state.ball.vy;
  frame(mockCtx, state);
  assert.notStrictEqual(state.ball.vy, oldVy, 'Ball velocity should have changed after brick collision');
});
```
Now `frame()` no longer handles collisions. It only draws.
The collision is handled in `step()`.
So `frame(mockCtx, state)` will NOT change the velocity.

I should update `game/collisions.test.js` to use `step()` instead of `frame()`.

